  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "With regards to the SDK, using rotation states is limiting with regards to stylized avatars. Some models may have one singular eye and other models might be better utilising positional offsets than rotation states. There's also specific scenarios where you want to rely on different rotational+positional offsets on each eye. It would also help to add parameters in the SDK that would be compatible with eye tracking software. I'm aware that there's OSC solutions but as some people have pointed out, it's a waste of parameter space to get it working properly on the network.",
